  "implementation": {
    "autonomous": "Sensor-code confidence in the 98-100% clipping shoulder, quantized to one byte per site. Protect admitted HL6 recovery and its neighbourhood. Interpolate confidence by CFA channel; after demosaic and before the colour matrix, lift channels with clipping evidence toward the maximum camera RGB. Preserve extended values without inferring clipping from RGB. Above explicit sensor clipping tags remains extended rather than marked clipped.",
    "AHD": "Capture unbalanced raw2image clipping confidence from local black and LibRaw nominal maximum. Post-interpolation callback applies the camera-RGB neutral fallback before colour conversion. AHD demosaic, highlight=1 scaling and uint16 limits remain. Linear DNG without CFA keeps its previous path.",
    "cache": "Distinct recipe identities reject previous autonomous/AHD artifacts.",
    "other_engines": "Apple, LibRaw bilinear and legacy TrueRenderer rendering algorithms unchanged.",
    "cost": "One confidence byte per sensor site, temporary coarse support maps in the autonomous engine and an extra raw2image preparation in AHD. No controlled performance comparison performed in this campaign."
  },
